ing everybody and and  the reopening is affecting  everybody as well i mean it's in some  places it's going to be quite slow and  there's even some businesses  like restaurants who are maybe limited  to 25  capacity who think i can't make a profit  with 25  capacity so they might not open at all  okay so this is where it's  you don't go down party lines ideology  you go down  adults versus children this is an  issue in which you have you are facing  supremely adult  questions adults unlike children  have to discuss risk and benefits every  day of their decisions  children don't so i have a new law i  call it the essie cup law  in honor of the reigning queen of adding  nothing to a conversation  until it's over so when chris christie  says  or tries to make the adult point that  late these future decisions regarding  lockdowns they're gonna carry a risk  of death then you'll see the cowardly  gawker  with no skin in the game again who makes  no adult decisions  will say hmm he'll be there to pick it  off and go  but people will die you are insensitive  to death  and you should go to a crowded place and  feed the hungry  because you don't care so that is the  childlike answer every time  and i think we could save our viewers a  lot of time  if we just cancel out these obvious  points like  adults know that every death is too much  right we know that  we also know that opening up is going to  increase risk  we also accept and share the risk every  day with different  actions so if your argument still lives  in that territory  you are a child and you should not be  allowed at the adults table  when we are talking about these  decisions so if you say that there is a  risk  the media will accuse you of murder no  matter what because they're children  when the states reopen and the leaders  are taking a calculated risk  blue or red state we have to give them  the leeway and not accuse them of murder  because that's infantile because we know  we're we're  adults we've lived